<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isingoma Mpuga Rukidi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rukidi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isingoma Mpuga Rukidi is remembered in tradition as the first king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babito-dynasty">Babito dynasty</a> of Bunyoro-Kitara. The stories present him as a Luo prince from the north who took over the lands of the departed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chwezi">Chwezi</a>, adopted their regalia and rituals and claimed to be their heir; his twin brother is said to have founded the Buganda kingship in some versions. Historians regard the details and dates as uncertain.</p></div>
